@startuml seq-lore-once
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 210
skinparam wrapWidth 190
skinparam shadowing false
title Chat lore — materialized once, sent once\n(spec: flows.spec.ts · "LLM synchronization — excludeFromContext flag in the request builder")
' Aliases match docs/specs/component-map.puml.

actor User
participant "SVC_LORE\nChatLoreService" as LORE
participant "SVC_CHAT\nChatService" as SVC
participant "ORCH_CONTEXT\nbuildSendMessagesEx()" as CTX
participant "flows/sends\nsend flow" as FLOW
participant "PORT\nChatApiPort" as API

== 1. Nobody has to write the lore into the thread ==
User -> SVC : patchChatMeta(chatId, {lore: 'Ashley is married to Dr. Harvey.'})
note right of SVC
  Chat.lore is ONE free-text blob — it is never a node the
  author has to edit. flows.spec asserts chat.lore stays
  untouched by any send.
end note

== 2. Before a direction is sent, one lore node is materialized ==
User -> FLOW : send a direction
FLOW -> LORE : ensureLoreNodeBefore(chatId, directionId, planSlice?)
LORE -> LORE : buildLoreNodeContent(lore, planSlice)
note right of LORE
  returns prefix + lore + suffix:
  [Current chat-lore — fixed canon …]
  …lore text…
  [/End of chat-lore]
  plus an OPTIONAL temporary section:
  [Chapter plan for this chapter — fixed canon …] … [/End of chapter plan]
  Blank / undefined lore ⇒ '' (no node at all).
end note
alt the direction already has a lore node as parent
  LORE -> SVC : patch that node's content (idempotent re-arm)
  note right of LORE
    re-arming with a DIFFERENT plan slice updates the SAME node;
    the old slice is gone, nothing accumulates.
  end note
else first send of this direction
  LORE -> SVC : addNode(role:'user', parent of the direction,\n content = wrapped lore)
  LORE -> SVC : patchNode(excludeAfterSend: true)
  note right of LORE
    excludeAfterSend = send it ONCE, then exclude it forever.
  end note
end
SVC -> API : createNode / patchNode

== 3. The send sees the lore, the chat does not change ==
FLOW -> CTX : buildSendMessagesEx({chatId, nodeId: direction})
CTX -> CTX : walk the path, skip excludeFromContext nodes,\nINCLUDE an excludeAfterSend node while it is still armed
CTX --> FLOW : messages[] containing the lore text
note right of CTX
  flows.spec: an excluded node is still sent while it IS the current
  question; a lore node is sent until it was sent, then flipped.
end note

== 4. After a real send the lore node is deactivated ==
FLOW -> LORE : markSentOnceExcluded(direction)
LORE -> SVC : patchNode(lore, excludeFromContext: true,\n excludeAfterSend: false)
FLOW -> CTX : buildSendMessagesEx() again
CTX --> FLOW : messages[] WITHOUT the lore text
note right of CTX
  so the canon costs tokens exactly once per direction, not
  once per turn — and the tree stays readable.
end note

== 5. The next direction gets a fresh node ==
User -> FLOW : send the next direction under the new answer
FLOW -> LORE : ensureLoreNodeBefore(chatId, nextDirectionId)
LORE -> SVC : addNode(…) — a NEW lore node (new id)
note right of LORE
  the old one stays deactivated; the new one carries the current
  plan slice. flows.spec asserts lore2.id ≠ lore1.id.
end note

== 6. Regenerate / rewrite / insert re-arm the shared lore ==
FLOW -> SVC : clear excludeFromContext on the lore node BEFORE the answer
note right of SVC
  flows.spec "send-regenerate / send-rewrite: clears the exclude flag
  … and re-sends the lore" and "send-insert: re-arms the shared lore
  node of the direction being inserted above".
  Re-generating an answer must not silently lose the canon.
end note

@enduml
